  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the continuation of Marinières beach, the Ange Gardien is a small, somewhat hidden pebble cove with views over the Villefranche bay. The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office simply describes it as "the Ange Gardien beach, located after the Marinières beach", listed among the beaches of Villefranche-sur-Mer along with Marinières, La Darse and Deux Rups.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office listing states "Pets are not accepted" at Ange Gardien beach, and answers "No" to the question "Are pets accepted at Plage de l'Ange Gardien?". The same mention appears on the listings of the Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur regional tourism committee and of Côte d'Azur France. Several unofficial directories and a 2023 press article nevertheless present a small pebble cove as open to dogs; no official source read confirms it.</p>
      <p>The tourist office's page on dog-allowed beaches lists seven beaches in the metropolitan area: in Villefranche-sur-Mer, only Deux Rups beach appears. The others are Cros dei Pin beach in Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat, Lenval and La Lanterne in Nice, Hippodrome beach in Cagnes-sur-Mer, Vespins beach in Saint-Laurent-du-Var and the Pointe des Douaniers in Cap-d'Ail. The page adds that outside these zones, dogs are not admitted on the other beaches of Nice Côte d'Azur. No municipal order from Villefranche-sur-Mer was found on the question.</p>
      <p>For a swim with your dog, neighbouring Deux Rups beach is therefore the one to favour. The leash is not specified on the Deux Rups listing: ask the town hall before coming.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: for a break with your dog in Villefranche, aim first for Deux Rups beach, the only one the tourist office cites.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old town of Villefranche, with its picturesque harbour and the Saint-Pierre chapel decorated by Cocteau, is worth a stroll after the swim. The tourist office can be reached on 04 93 01 73 68 for any question about the commune's beaches.</p>
